      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "To find the volume of the frustum, we first need to determine the volume of the original pyramid and the volume of the smaller pyramid that is removed to form the frustum.\n\nThe formula for the volume of a pyramid is given by:\n\n\\[\nV = \\frac{1}{3} \\cdot A \\cdot h\n\\]\n\nwhere \\( A \\) is the area of the base and \\( h \\) is the height of the pyramid.\n\n1. **Volume of the Original Pyramid:**\n\nFirst, we calculate the area of the base of the original pyramid. Since the original pyramid is a square pyramid with a base edge of 12 cm, its base area is:\n\n\\[\nA = 12 \\times 12 = 144 \\text{ cm}^2\n\\]\n\nThe height of the original pyramid also corresponds to 8 cm.\n\nThus, the volume of the original pyramid is:\n\n\\[\nV_{\\text{original}} = \\frac{1}{3} \\cdot 144 \\cdot 8 = \\frac{1}{3} \\cdot 1152 = 384 \\text{ cm}^3\n\\]\n\n2. **Volume of the Smaller Pyramid:**\n\nThe smaller pyramid has a base edge of 6 cm and an altitude of 4 cm. Its base area is given by:\n\n\\[\nA = 6 \\times 6 = 36 \\text{ cm}^2\n\\]\n\nAnd the height of the smaller pyramid is 4 cm.\n\nThe volume of the smaller pyramid is:\n\n\\displaystyle{V_{\\text{smaller}} = \\frac{1}{3} \\cdot 36 \\cdot 4 = \\frac{1}{3} \\cdot 144 = 48 \\text{ cm}^3}\n\\]\n\n3. **Volume of the Frustum:**\n\nThe volume of the frustum is obtained by subtracting the volume of the smaller pyramid from the volume of the original, i.e.,\n\n\\[\nV_{\\text{frustum}} = V_{\\text{original}} - V_{\\text{smaller}}\n\\]\n\nThus, we calculate the volume of the frustum:\n\n\\displaystyle{V_{\\text{frustum}} = 384 - 48 = 336 \\text{ cm}^3}\n\\]\n\nHence, the volume of the frustum in cubic centimeters is \\(\\boxed{336}\\).",
