      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "==Since the two pyramids are both similar to the original pyramid, we can find their heights and base edges and then use these to find the volume of the frustum by subtracting the volume of the smaller pyramid from the volume of the original pyramid==.\n\nThe volume of a pyramid is $\\frac{1}{3}(12^2)(8)=384$ cubic centimeters. $\\frac{6^2(4)}{6^2}(8)=192$ cubic centimeters. $\\boxed{192}$ cubic centimeters.",
