    {
      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "To find the volume of the frustum, we first calculate the volume of the entire pyramid and then subtract the volume of the smaller pyramid. The volume of a pyramid is given by \\( V = \\frac{1}{3} \\text{Base Area} \\times \\text{Height} \\).\n\nThe volume of the entire pyramid (larger pyramid) is:\n\\[ V_{\\text{large}} = \\frac{1}{3} \\times 12^2 \\times 8 = \\frac{1}{3} \\times 144 \\times 8 = 384 \\text{ cm}^3 \\]\n\nNext, we find the volume of the smaller pyramid using the same formula:\n\\[ V_{\\text{small}} = \\frac{1}{3} \\times 6^2 \\times 4 = \\frac{1}{3} \\times 36 \\times 4 = 48 \\text{ cm}^3 \\]\n\nFinally, we subtract the volume of the smaller pyramid from the volume of the larger pyramid to get the volume of the frustum:\n\\[ V_{\\text{frustum}} = V_{\\text{large}} - V_{\\text{small}} = 384 - 48 = 336 \\text{ cm}^3 \\]\n\nSo, the volume of the frustum is 336 cubic centimeters.",
